  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;DUTCH WATERCOLORIST LIEN VERBURGT-KRAMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lien Verburgt-Kramers is a Dutch watercolorist born in 1876 and passed away in 1968, known for her remarkable achievements in the art world and her contributions to bridging the gender gap."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WIKIMEDIA PROJECT NL GENDERGAP MAINTENANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NL Gendergap maintenance is a project aimed at increasing the representation of women on Wikipedia, addressing the gender imbalance in the online encyclopedia."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. SASKIA WOUTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Saskia Wouters is a historian and a member of the NL Gendergap maintenance project, committed to recognizing and celebrating the achievements of women."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. SOPHIA PATEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Sophia Patel is a leading expert on Lien Verburgt-Kramers' life and work, uncovering her connection to badminton."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WIKIPROJECT BADMINTON/TOURNAMENT FOCUS LIST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The WikiProject Badminton/tournament focus list is a project aimed at improving the coverage of badminton tournaments on Wikipedia."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RACHEL LEE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rachel Lee is the coordinator of the WikiProject Badminton/tournament focus list, excited to explore Verburgt-Kramers' unique connection to badminton."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SANDRA RIENTJES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sandra Rientjes is the Chair of Wikimedia Netherlands, supporting initiatives that promote gender equality."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WIKIPEDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wikipedia is an online encyclopedia where the NL Gendergap maintenance project aims to increase the representation of women."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BADMINTON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Badminton is a fast-paced racquet sport in which Lien Verburgt-Kramers was a skilled player and participant in local tournaments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Badminton is an activity that Verburgt-Kramers is interested in, as evidenced by the tweet."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ART WORLD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Art World is the field in which Lien Verburgt-Kramers made significant contributions as a watercolorist."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL TOURNAMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Local Tournaments are events where Lien Verburgt-Kramers participated in badminton, showcasing her skills in the sport."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NETHERLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Netherlands is the country where Lien Verburgt-Kramers lived and worked, and where she participated in local badminton tournaments."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARCHIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Archives contain letters exchanged between Verburgt-Kramers and her niece, revealing her passion for badminton."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LETTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ARTIFACT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Letters exchanged between Verburgt-Kramers and her niece, providing insight into her interest in badminton."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NIECE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Verburgt-Kramers' niece was an avid badminton player, corresponding with Verburgt-Kramers about the sport."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOCIAL MEDIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Social Media platforms are used by art enthusiasts and badminton fans to share their thoughts and reactions to Verburgt-Kramers' badminton connection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Social media platforms are where reactions and thoughts about Verburgt-Kramers' badminton interest are shared."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ART ENTHUSIASTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Art Enthusiasts are followers of Lien Verburgt-Kramers' work and are interested in her life and legacy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Art enthusiasts are interested in Verburgt-Kramers' artistic work and are now learning about her interest in badminton."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BADMINTON FANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Badminton Fans are followers of the sport and are interested in Verburgt-Kramers' connection to the sport."&lt;SEP&gt;"Badminton fans are interested in Verburgt-Kramers' interest in badminton and are sharing their thoughts on social media."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENDER IMBALANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gender Imbalance refers to the long-standing issue of underrepresentation of women in the art world and on Wikipedia."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLLABORATIVE EFFORTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Collaborative Efforts refer to the joint efforts of organizations and individuals to promote gender equality and recognize women's achievements."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECOGNITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Recognition refers to the acknowledgment and celebration of women's achievements in various fields."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PASSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Passion refers to the driving force behind Verburgt-Kramers' involvement in both art and badminton."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VERBURGT-KRAMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Verburgt-Kramers is an artist known for her work, and she has a lesser-known interest in badminton."</data>
